WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.269
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:06.340
DINO CHIESA: Dino here.

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:09.370
Now we're going to learn how
to add API key verification

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:11.440
to any API proxy.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.690
If you haven't done the work
in the prior video, where

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:16.750
you created your first
proxy, stop here and go back

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.800
and watch that video now.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:25.200
In the Apigee UI, select the
proxy we created previously.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.730
Click the Develop tab.

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:30.550
Now, click the Preflow
in the proxy endpoint

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:34.430
and click the plus step icon.

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:39.670
Scroll down and select
the Verify API Key Policy.

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:42.820
Click Add, and done.

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:47.110
Now I've added API key
verification to my proxy.

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:49.360
Every request that is
received by this proxy

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:52.720
will need to send a key.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:55.620
What happens when I
invoke our test proxy?

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:59.210
Well, you can see
I get an error.

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:01.520
The Apigee proxy is
rejecting the request

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:05.440
because I didn't
pass an API key.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:08.350
How can we generate
a valid API key?

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:11.170
Let me show you.

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:14.810
Let's flip back
to the Apigee UI.

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:20.090
The first step is to wrap
that proxy in an API product.

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:22.280
In Apigee Edge,
the API product is

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:27.080
the way we expose APIs
to consuming developers.

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:32.510
Click the Publish menu, API
products, click plus API

00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:37.850
product, name it, and include
the API proxy we just created.

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:43.560
Click Save.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:46.020
Now we need a developer.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:48.120
Normally, developers
add themselves

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:50.970
via the developer portal,
but we can also do it here

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:54.480
in the administrative UI.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:02:00.500
Click Publish, developers,
plus developer.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:05.050
Specify the relevant
information.

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:09.840
Now create an app that is
authorized for that product.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:16.380
Click Publish, Apps,
plus app, name the app,

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:22.810
select a developer, and
add the API product.

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:23.455
Click Save.

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:28.650
Click back in to
see the details,

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:34.310
and we see the consumer key,
also known as the API key.

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:37.730
Let's copy that.

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:39.170
Flip tabs.

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:42.780
Paste in the key as
a query parameter

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:45.150
and invoke the API again.

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:48.450
You can see the API proxy
is now allowing the request

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:50.520
with the valid API key.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:52.500
The key ideas here--

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.970
products wrap API proxies.

00:02:55.970 --> 00:02:59.960
Apps have API keys that are
authorized for specific API

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:01.760
products.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.830
Developers own those apps.

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:09.710
In this video, we learned
the concept of an API product

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:14.670
and we added a verify API
key policy to our API proxy.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:17.490
Verify API key is just
one of over 30 policies

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:19.680
built into Apigee Edge.

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:21.850
Simply selecting
from a dropdown list,

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:24.660
you can add policies for
traffic management, security,

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:26.640
and message manipulation.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:29.430
You can also write custom
logic in JavaScript or Python

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:32.530
or even Java if you
need something special.

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:37.270
You have full control over the
request and response messages.

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:39.070
There's a lot of power here.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:40.780
To help you learn
about it all, don't

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:45.580
forget the documentation and
the community sites for Apigee.

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:48.040
Be sure to watch the next
video in this series, where

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:51.250
we'll cover tracing and
the assign message policy.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:53.110
Until then, keep it digital.

00:03:53.110 --> 00:03:56.460
[MUSIC PLAYING]

